00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:17.290
<i>He's in trouble.</i>

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.330
<i>He's hurting now that the 
two-syllable cards are one-syllable.</i>

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:22.260
<i>This is how the Master 
plays when he's serious!</i>

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:25.260
After I win my fifth consecutive title,
 I'm going to retire.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.530
The Master takes the lead for 
the first time this match.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:32.110
Can he widen it even further?

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.500
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:37.880
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:42.850
<i>If you ask me, your karuta 
style is very simplistic.</i>

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:47.250
<i>You're just fortifying your own side
with cards that are easy for you to take.</i>

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.170
<i>That's why...</i>

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.650
<i>As the first frost...</i>

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:52.540
<i>His hand was low on that cover! Smart!</i>

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:54.040
<i>That's normal, though...</i>

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.950
<i>The hazed early dawn light comes not...</i>

